# Stalwart — legacy `config.toml` reference (pre-v0.16)

> **This template no longer applies to the v0.16 image.** Since v0.16, Stalwart does not
> generate or consume a bootstrap `config.toml`. It writes a small datastore-oriented
> `config.json` into `/etc/stalwart` and all management/configuration lives in JMAP
> objects (admin UI and `stalwart-cli` both use JMAP). See `docs/infra/STALWART.md`.

This file is kept as a historical reference for older Stalwart versions and to document
the listener/TLS/postgres intent that now lives in JMAP datastore configuration:

```toml
[server]
hostname = "mx1.guidedstepswellness.com"
max-connections = 8192

[server.tls]
enable = true
implicit = true
certificate = "file:///opt/stalwart/certs/fullchain.pem"
private-key = "file:///opt/stalwart/certs/privkey.pem"

[authentication.fallback-admin]
user = "admin"
secret = "<ADMIN_PASSWORD>"

# --- Listeners ---
[server.listener.https]
bind = "[::]:443"
protocol = "http"
tls.implicit = true

[server.listener.http]
bind = "[::]:8080"
protocol = "http"

[server.listener.smtp]
bind = "[::]:25"
protocol = "smtp"

[server.listener.submissions]
bind = "[::]:465"
protocol = "smtp"
tls.implicit = true

[server.listener.submission]
bind = "[::]:587"
protocol = "smtp"

[server.listener.imap]
bind = "[::]:143"
protocol = "imap"

[server.listener.imaptls]
bind = "[::]:993"
protocol = "imap"
tls.implicit = true

[server.listener.sieve]
bind = "[::]:4190"
protocol = "managesieve"

# --- Product store: PostgreSQL (alternative to default RocksDB) ---
[store.postgresql_cluster]
type = "postgresql"
host = "postgres"
port = 5432
database = "stalwart_mail"
user = "<STALWART_DB_USER>"
password = "<STALWART_DB_PASSWORD>"
pool.max-connections = 10

[storage]
data = "postgresql_cluster"
blob = "postgresql_cluster"
fts = "postgresql_cluster"
lookup = "postgresql_cluster"
directory = "postgresql_cluster"
```

## What changed in v0.16 (recreate these in JMAP)
- Listener/TLS settings → JMAP configuration objects.
- PostgreSQL storage → configure each `storage.*` cluster in the datastore directories.
- The anti-abuse and admin-port guidance below still applies.

## Notes
- The official Docker image uses named volumes (RocksDB) for local development; switch
  the datastore to a PostgreSQL cluster for production hosting via the admin UI/JMAP.
- When the outbound path migrates to a relay inside Stalwart (not the MVP), a relay
  route is configured as a JMAP routing object.
- Gate admin surfaces behind the security boundary: 443 terminates TLS, 8080 binds to
  loopback only, and Postgres/Stalwart internals are never published to the internet.